<title>GERMANY: Veba details nine-month 1996 results.</title>
<headline>Veba details nine-month 1996 results.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to September 30 (in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			   1,227   vs 980</p>
<p>    Group sales				  55,310  vs 54,554</p>
<p>Group net profit (incl. minorities)	1,407   vs 1,153</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit		     2,513   vs 2,191</p>
<p>    Group tax payment			  1,106   vs 1,038</p>
<p>    Group investment			   3,690   vs 2,902</p>
<p>    Group workforce			    123,388 vs 125,158</p>
<p>Breakdown of sales:</p>
<p>    Electricity				  11,178  vs 11,466</p>
<p>    Chemicals				    8,054   vs 8,355</p>
<p>    Oil					    12,873  vs 11,734</p>
<p>    Trade/transport/services		 22,923  vs 22,728</p>
<p>    Telecommunications			 282     vs 271</p>
<p>Breakdown in investment:</p>
<p>    Electricity				  1,242   vs 1,560</p>
<p>    Chemicals				    1,275   vs 500</p>
<p>    Oil					    147     vs 60</p>
<p>    Trade/transport/services		 843     vs 561</p>
<p>    Telecommunications			 183     vs 221</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German diversified energy, chemicals and services group is Veba AG. Analysts had expected group net profits to come out around 1.1 billion marks, with pre-tax profits forecast at 2.35 billion marks. Workforce figures compare position at end September 1996 with numbers at end of December 1995.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
